Sat Nov 14 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Testing branch: show the Agama web UI in Scuttler, a Qt WebEngine
  shell, instead of Firefox in GNOME Kiosk. scuttler-kiosk runs it as
  the unprivileged scuttler user in a KWin session on tty1 and passes
  the Agama token as a systemd credential. Based on Kalpa's
  kalpa-installer PR 7.
- Drop MozillaFirefox, its branding, gdm-systemd, gnome-shell,
  gnome-session-wayland and gnome-kiosk.
- Remove only Qt 5 libraries in config.sh; Scuttler needs Qt 6.
- Remove the GNOME Kiosk scripts, the Firefox profile and extension,
  the GDM autologin, the AccountsService root session, the dconf
  appearance settings and agama-screenshot (it used GNOME Shell).
- Keep the dark scheme with a scuttler.service drop-in that sets
  blink's preferredColorScheme. High contrast is not carried over.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 10 01:30:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Stop downloading the NVIDIA open driver into the Offline image during
  the build. OBS build workers have no network, so config.sh failed and
  the Offline ISO never built. NVIDIA's userspace is not on OBS.
- Offline media relies on Agama probing the product's online
  repositories (agama #4189, in the agama snapshot this image uses).
  atropos-agama-config adds the NVIDIA repository at priority 200 only
  when it answers within ten seconds; Agama does not probe extra
  repositories, and an unreachable one fails the solve.
- The configuration service waits for network-online.target.
- List curl in the image for that probe.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 10 00:30:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- List patch in the Offline image. flatpak-builder needs
  /usr/bin/patch, which patch and busybox-patch both provide, and OBS
  left the image unresolvable on that choice. The pattern's Requires
  did not settle it; OBS only checks packages named in the kiwi file.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Nov 07 17:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Install atropos-agama-post through the kiwi file list. KIWI does not
  copy other package files to /image, so config.sh failed and the
  online ISO did not build.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Nov 07 15:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Add atropos-agama-post as an Agama post-installation script. It adds
  compress=zstd:-4 and lazytime to the root line in /etc/fstab, which
  Agama did not write from the product file, and removes the live
  ISO options Agama copies into /etc/kernel/cmdline: live.*, an empty
  security=, a root= naming the LUKS partition, and the silent-boot
  options that atropos-performance already adds.
- Build the installer defaults with jq for both flavors.

